                    <h1 class="content-title">Audit & <span class="gradient-text">Regulatory Change</span></h1>
                    <p class="content-subtitle">
                        Two critical IRM modules that help organizations stay ahead of compliance — Audit Management 
                        for internal assurance, and Regulatory Change Management for tracking the evolving regulatory landscape.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Audit Overview -->
                <section class="content-section" id="audit-overview">
                    <h2>Audit Management Overview</h2>
                    <p>
                        The <strong>Audit Management</strong> module automates the entire internal audit process — 
                        from annual planning through fieldwork to final reporting. It integrates with Policy & Compliance 
                        to leverage existing control data and with Risk Management to ensure audits are risk-driven.
                    </p>

                    <h3>Key Capabilities</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Risk-Based Audit Planning:</strong> Prioritize audit engagements based on risk scores from the IRM risk register</li>
                        <li><strong>Resource Management:</strong> Track auditor availability, skills, and workload allocation</li>
                        <li><strong>Test Plans & Templates:</strong> Create reusable test procedures that align with your audit methodology</li>
                        <li><strong>Automated Evidence Requests:</strong> Send targeted evidence requests to control owners with built-in follow-ups</li>
                        <li><strong>Real-Time Dashboards:</strong> Track audit project status, findings, and resource utilization</li>
                        <li><strong>Integration with Compliance:</strong> Leverage existing control assessments to reduce duplicated testing</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <!-- Audit Lifecycle -->
                <section class="content-section" id="audit-lifecycle">
                    <h2>Audit Lifecycle</h2>
                    <p>
                        An audit engagement follows a structured lifecycle that mirrors standard internal audit methodology:
                    </p>

                    <div class="diagram-block">
                        <div class="diagram-title">Audit Engagement Lifecycle</div>
                        <div class="flow-container">
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">01</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Planning</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Define scope, objectives, resources</span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">02</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Fieldwork</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Execute tests, collect evidence</span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">03</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Reporting</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Document findings & recommendations</span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">04</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Follow-Up</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Track remediation & validate fixes</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="accordion">
                        <div class="accordion-item open">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Phase 1: Planning</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p>
                                        The planning phase establishes the audit universe and creates the annual audit plan. 
                                        Key activities include:
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        • Define audit objectives and scope<br>
                                        • Identify in-scope entities, controls, and risk areas<br>
                                        • Allocate audit resources (team members, hours)<br>
                                        • Create the audit engagement record and timeline<br>
                                        • Develop test plans using templates or custom test procedures
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Phase 2: Fieldwork</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p>
                                        Fieldwork is where the actual testing happens. Auditors execute test procedures, 
                                        collect evidence, and document their observations. Key activities include:
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        • Execute control tests against defined test procedures<br>
                                        • Send and track evidence requests to control owners<br>
                                        • Review evidence and document working papers<br>
                                        • Record test results (Effective, Ineffective, Not Tested)<br>
                                        • Document preliminary findings
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Phase 3: Reporting</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p>
                                        Findings are formalized, rated by severity, and compiled into audit reports:
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        • Create formal audit findings with severity ratings<br>
                                        • Develop recommendations and management responses<br>
                                        • Generate audit report with executive summary<br>
                                        • Obtain management acknowledgment and agreement on remediation timelines<br>
                                        • Distribute report to stakeholders
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Phase 4: Follow-Up</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p>
                                        After the audit report is issued, remediation activities are tracked:
                                    </p>
                                    <p>
                                        • Track remediation task progress against agreed timelines<br>
                                        • Send escalation notifications for overdue items<br>
                                        • Validate remediation effectiveness through re-testing<br>
                                        • Close findings when remediation is verified<br>
                                        • Generate follow-up reports for audit committee
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Audit Workspace -->
                <section class="content-section" id="audit-workspace">
                    <h2>Audit Workspace</h2>
                    <p>
                        The <strong>Audit Workspace</strong> is a persona-based interface that provides different 
                        views depending on the user's role:
                    </p>

                    <div class="data-table-wrapper">
                        <table class="data-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Persona</th>
                                    <th>View Focus</th>
                                    <th>Key Widgets</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Chief Audit Executive</strong></td>
                                    <td>Strategic overview, resource utilization, audit universe</td>
                                    <td>Annual plan progress, finding trends, risk coverage heatmap</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Audit Manager</strong></td>
                                    <td>Project management, team allocation, engagement status</td>
                                    <td>Active engagements, resource calendar, overdue findings</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Auditor</strong></td>
                                    <td>Daily work, assigned tests, evidence review</td>
                                    <td>My tasks, evidence requests, test results, working papers</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Auditee (Business Owner)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Requests requiring attention, finding remediation</td>
                                    <td>Open evidence requests, assigned remediations, upcoming audits</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Evidence -->
                <section class="content-section" id="evidence">
                    <h2>Evidence Collection</h2>
                    <p>
                        Evidence collection in IRM is partially automated. The system can:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Auto-generate evidence requests</strong> when test procedures are initiated</li>
                        <li><strong>Send reminder notifications</strong> for pending evidence requests</li>
                        <li><strong>Escalate</strong> overdue requests to managers</li>
                        <li><strong>Link evidence</strong> to specific controls, tests, and findings for full traceability</li>
                        <li><strong>Attach files</strong> including screenshots, documents, and system exports</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--tip">
                        <div class="info-card-title">Developer Tip</div>
                        <p>
                            Use <strong>Flow Designer</strong> to customize evidence request workflows. Common 
                            customizations include auto-attaching supporting data from indicator results, routing 
                            requests based on control owner department, and adding approval steps before evidence 
                            is accepted.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- RCM Overview -->
                <section class="content-section" id="rcm-overview">
                    <h2>Regulatory Change Management (RCM)</h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Regulatory Change Management</strong> is designed for organizations operating in 
                        heavily regulated industries (financial services, healthcare, energy) where the regulatory 
                        landscape is constantly evolving.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        RCM helps answer critical questions:
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>What new regulations are coming that affect us?</li>
                        <li>Which of our policies and controls need to be updated?</li>
                        <li>What's the gap between our current compliance state and the new requirements?</li>
                        <li>Who needs to be involved in implementing changes?</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <!-- RCM Workflow -->
                <section class="content-section" id="rcm-workflow">
                    <h2>RCM Workflow</h2>
                    <p>
                        The regulatory change management process follows a structured workflow:
                    </p>

                    <div class="diagram-block">
                        <div class="diagram-title">Regulatory Change Workflow</div>
                        <div class="flow-container">
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">01</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Ingest</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Receive regulatory alerts from intelligence sources</span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">02</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Triage</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Categorize and determine relevance</span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">03</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Assess</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Evaluate impact on policies, controls, entities</span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">04</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Implement</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Update policies, controls, processes</span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
                            <div class="flow-step">
                                <span class="flow-step-num">05</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-label">Verify</span>
                                <span class="flow-step-desc">Confirm compliance with new requirements</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Key RCM Concepts</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Regulatory Alerts:</strong> Incoming notifications from regulatory intelligence 
                            providers (e.g., Thomson Reuters, Wolters Kluwer). These are ingested and centralized 
                            in the platform.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Taxonomy Mapping:</strong> Different regulatory providers use different classification 
                            systems. RCM allows you to map multiple provider taxonomies to your single internal taxonomy, 
                            enabling consistent processing regardless of source.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Impact Assessment Playbooks:</strong> Guided questionnaires configured by compliance 
                            teams to systematically evaluate how a regulatory change affects different business areas.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Change Campaigns:</strong> When a regulatory change requires updates across multiple 
                            policies, controls, or processes, a campaign coordinates all the tasks, approvals, and 
                            verifications needed.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <!-- AI in RCM -->
                <section class="content-section" id="rcm-ai">
                    <h2>AI & Machine Learning in RCM</h2>
                    <p>
                        ServiceNow leverages AI/ML capabilities to reduce the manual burden of regulatory 
                        change management:
                    </p>

                    <div class="accordion">
                        <div class="accordion-item open">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">AI Compliance Mapping</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p>
                                        ML models can automatically suggest mappings between new regulatory requirements 
                                        and existing internal citations, policies, and controls. This dramatically reduces 
                                        the time compliance teams spend manually analyzing new regulations.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Predictive Insights</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p>
                                        Based on historical patterns, AI can predict which areas of the organization 
                                        are most likely to be impacted by certain types of regulatory changes, helping 
                                        compliance teams proactively prepare rather than reactively scramble.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item">
                            <button class="accordion-trigger">
                                <span class="accordion-trigger-text">Automated Categorization</span>
                                <span class="accordion-icon">▾</span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                <div class="accordion-content">
                                    <p>
                                        Incoming regulatory alerts can be automatically categorized by topic, jurisdiction, 
                                        and urgency using NLP (Natural Language Processing) models. This speeds up the 
                                        triage process and ensures critical changes aren't lost in the noise.
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--warning">
                        <div class="info-card-title">Note</div>
                        <p>
                            Advanced AI features in RCM may require specific premium plugins and licensing. 
                            Check your ServiceNow licensing agreement to understand which AI capabilities 
                            are available in your instance.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

